-- A kind of surveyed thing (site, plot, specimen) names its parent kind.
-- The nearest kind up the tree that records a location is where a
-- specimen's location comes from: a walk (Reference §7, "Walks"). A kind is
-- never its own ancestor: a prohibition reading the named walk. `parent` is
-- fixed when the kind is created, so the prohibition is checked at the door.
act Kind {
    name: text
    parent: one Kind?
    hasLocation: boolean

    ancestors: many Kind = walk parent
    locationHolder: one Kind? = walk parent until hasLocation
}

never (Kind where count(Kind where name == this.name) > 1)
never (Kind where this in ancestors) tolerates contention
